	<h2 id="service">4. Description of the Service</h2>
	<p>Stockpile provides software that lets you:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>browse news stories and curated "bags", which are editorial baskets of tokenized stocks and pre-IPO tokens with suggested weights;</li>
		<li>view what each bag holds, along with prices, charts, and sources;</li>
		<li>buy or sell a bag's tokens through swaps routed by Jupiter, signed by your own embedded wallet;</li>
		<li>see your portfolio, activity, and per-bag performance; and</li>
		<li>save bags for later.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Stockpile does not issue, hold, custody, or sell any token, and it is not the counterparty to your trades. Swaps run on the
		Solana blockchain against third-party liquidity.
	</p>

	<h2 id="no-advice">5. Not investment advice</h2>
	<p>
		Bags, weights, stories, summaries, charts, and disclosure data are provided for information only. They are not investment,
		financial, legal, or tax advice, and they are not a recommendation or solicitation to buy or sell anything. Bags are not funds,
		indexes, or managed portfolios, and they are not rebalanced for you. Past performance does not indicate future results. We owe
		you no fiduciary duty. Consider getting independent advice before making any investment decision.
	</p>

	<h2 id="tokens">6. Tokenized assets and issuers</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>What you hold.</strong> xStocks are tokenized certificates issued by Backed that track listed equities. PreStocks are
			SPV-based tokens that reference private-company valuations. Holding these tokens does not make you a shareholder. You get no
			voting, dividend, or information rights in the underlying company unless the issuer's terms expressly say so.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Issuer terms govern.</strong> Each token is subject to its issuer's terms, prospectus, and disclosures. The issuer, not
			Stockpile, is responsible for the token, its backing, redemption, and corporate actions.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Issuer risk.</strong> If an issuer, custodian, or SPV fails, is hacked, or stops operating, your tokens may lose some or
			all of their value, and Stockpile cannot make you whole.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Price divergence.</strong> On-chain token prices can differ from exchange or issuer reference prices, especially outside
			market hours, during volatility, or when liquidity is thin.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="third-parties">7. Third-party services</h2>
	<p>Stockpile integrates with these providers for core features:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Jupiter</strong>: we use Jupiter's swap API to aggregate and route token swaps across Solana decentralized exchanges and
			liquidity venues, and for token metadata and prices.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Privy</strong>: we use Privy for sign-in and embedded, self-custodial wallet infrastructure. Your wallet's keys are
			managed by Privy's key-management system, not by Stockpile.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Helius</strong>: we use Helius for Solana RPC access, reading balances and history, simulating transactions, and relaying them.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Backed (xStocks)</strong> and <strong>PreStocks</strong>: they issue the tokenized assets shown in bags.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Data providers</strong> such as tokens.xyz, Pyth Network, and CongressInvests: they supply charts, reference prices, and
			public disclosure data.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		By using Stockpile's swap, wallet, and trading features, you also agree to the terms of service of these providers,
		including <a href="https://jup.ag/terms-of-use" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jupiter's Terms of Use</a> and
