	</p>

	<h2 id="self-custody">8. Self-custody and your wallet</h2>
	<p>
		Stockpile is non-custodial. Your wallet and its assets belong to you, and Stockpile cannot access your keys, move your funds,
		reverse transactions, or recover a lost wallet. You are solely responsible for:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>keeping your sign-in email, device, and any wallet export or recovery method secure;</li>
		<li>every transaction you approve from your wallet; and</li>
		<li>any loss caused by unauthorized access to your email, device, or wallet.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="transactions">9. Quotes, transactions, and fees</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Quotes are indicative.</strong> Prices, routes, and price impact come from Jupiter and on-chain liquidity and may change
			between quote and execution. Slippage limits apply, and a swap can fail, or fill differently than shown, when the market moves.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Buying a bag means several swaps.</strong> A bag purchase is a series of separate transactions, one per token. Some legs
			may succeed while others fail, so you may end up holding only part of a bag.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>You sign every transaction.</strong> Transactions are prepared by our API, checked on your device, and signed by your
			wallet. Once signed, we relay them to the Solana network. Confirmed transactions are final and irreversible.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Network fee sponsorship.</strong> Stockpile currently pays Solana network fees and token-account rent for eligible swaps.
			Sponsorship is at our discretion, has limits, and may change or end at any time.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Fees.</strong> Stockpile does not currently charge its own fee on swaps. Jupiter routes, liquidity venues, and issuers
			may build fees or spreads into prices. If we introduce a Stockpile fee, we will show it before you confirm a trade.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="content">10. Content and data accuracy</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>News.</strong> Stories are summarized from third-party publishers, sometimes with the help of automated and AI tools, and
			may contain errors or omissions. The original articles belong to their publishers.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Disclosure bags.</strong> STOCK Act filings are published 30 to 45 days after a trade, report value ranges rather than
			exact amounts, and may include trades by spouses. Disclosure bags are built from public records. They are not a live or managed
			portfolio, and no member of Congress endorses or is affiliated with Stockpile.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Market data.</strong> Prices, charts, and performance figures may be delayed, estimated, or unavailable. Do not rely on
			them as the sole basis for any decision.
		</li>
	</ul>

